.TH _PRINTF 3 "April 2026" "Holberton School" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
_printf \- custom implementation of printf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include \(dqmain.h\(dq.br
.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
_printf writes output to stdout according to a format string.
The format string is composed of zero or more directives.
.PP
The following conversion specifiers are supported:
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a string. If the argument is NULL, prints "(null)".
.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints a signed decimal integer.
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters printed (excluding the null byte used to end output).

Returns -1 if the format string is NULL.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
_printf("Hello %s!\n", "World");
_printf("Character: %c\n", 'A');
_printf("Integer: %d, %i\n", 42, -42);
_printf("Percent sign: %%\n");
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only the following specifiers are supported: %c, %s, %d, %i, and %%.
Flags, field width, precision, length modifiers, and other specifiers are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
printf(3)
.SH BUGS
No known bugs.
